---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '@lib/config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Financial Disclaimer | CalcFalcon"
  description="CalcFalcon's calculators are estimation tools, not tax, financial, or investment advice. Read our full disclaimer before relying on any result."
>
  <div class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h1 class="heading-lg mb-4">Financial Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="text-neutral-600 text-lg mb-8">
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> August 9, 2026
      </p>

      <div class="card-elevated p-6 md:p-8 mb-10 border-l-4 border-finance-500">
        <p class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-2">In short: this is not advice.</p>
        <p class="text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
          Every calculator, article, and worked example on CalcFalcon is an educational estimation tool.
          Nothing on this site is tax, legal, investment, or financial advice, and using it does not create
          an advisory or professional relationship of any kind. Your specific situation almost certainly
          involves details a general-purpose calculator can't see. Before you file a return, make a
          quarterly payment, sell an asset, or make any other financial decision, confirm the numbers with
          a licensed CPA, tax attorney, enrolled agent, or financial advisor.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-neutral prose-lg max-w-none">
        <h2>Why We Publish This</h2>
        <p>
          Freelance income, self-employment tax, capital gains, and retirement planning fall into what the
          industry calls "Your Money or Your Life" (YMYL) content — topics where bad information can cause
          real financial harm. We take that seriously. This page exists so you know exactly what our
          calculators are, and are not, before you rely on a single number they produce.
        </p>

        <h2>What Our Calculators Do</h2>
        <p>
          Every calculator on CalcFalcon applies published formulas — IRS tax brackets, FICA rates, platform
          fee structures, compound interest math — to the numbers you enter. They run entirely in your
          browser. See our <a href="/methodology" class="text-primary-600 hover:underline">methodology page</a>
          for exactly how each calculator is built and sourced.
        </p>

        <h2>What Our Calculators Don't Do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>They don't know your full financial picture — dependents, prior-year carryovers, state-specific rules, credits, or deductions you haven't entered.</li>
          <li>They don't account for every edge case in the tax code, platform fee schedule, or interest calculation they model.</li>
          <li>They don't replace a professional's judgment. A CPA or financial advisor can ask follow-up questions a calculator cannot.</li>
          <li>They can be wrong. Inputs can be mistyped, formulas can have bugs despite our best effort, and published rates change. See our <a href="/methodology" class="text-primary-600 hover:underline">correction policy</a> if you spot an error.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Tax and Legal Rules Change</h2>
        <p>
          Tax brackets, contribution limits, and thresholds are adjusted annually and can change through new
          legislation at any time. Each tax and finance calculator on this site shows a "Sources &amp;
          Last Updated" block citing which tax year the figures reflect and when we last checked them against
          the IRS. If you are reading this after that date, confirm current figures directly with the IRS or
          your tax professional before acting.
        </p>

        <h2>No Investment Recommendations</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on CalcFalcon recommends buying, selling, or holding any specific investment, security, or
          financial product. Where we link to third-party financial products (see our
          <a href="/about#how-we-make-money" class="text-primary-600 hover:underline">affiliate disclosure</a>),
          those links are compensated referrals, not endorsements of suitability for your situation.
        </p>

        <h2>No Professional Relationship</h2>
        <p>
          Using this site, subscribing to our newsletter, or contacting us does not create a
          client, advisory, fiduciary, or professional relationship between you and CalcFalcon or its authors.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          CalcFalcon and its operators are not liable for decisions made using information from this site. See
          our full <a href="/terms" class="text-primary-600 hover:underline">Terms of Service</a> for the
          complete limitation of liability.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions or Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Spotted a figure that looks outdated or wrong? Please tell us — <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-primary-600 hover:underline">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
          or via our <a href="/contact" class="text-primary-600 hover:underline">contact form</a>. We would
          rather fix it than have it stand.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
